            {
                "entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                "word": "girolle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d7eba45c-f445-4bcd-b1cc-153b76531d7e",
                        "entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "girolles"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "02ebf728-5ba0-4b1c-958f-ac6f87129fae",
                        "entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "girole"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "00c78871-c1fb-373c-bbf9-9e6da51aeac1",
                        "entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Espèce de champignons à plis lamelliformes, au chapeau convexe, s’aplatissant, puis en entonnoir, jaune plus ou moins orangé, au pied sans anneau, concolore et aux spores jaune pâle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "953a8089-f012-439b-a138-3334b018cc7a",
                                "sense_id": "00c78871-c1fb-373c-bbf9-9e6da51aeac1",
                                "text": "Avec une fierté évidente, elle déposa au centre de la table un long plat de faïence ovale et courut à la cuisine chercher une casserolette de cuivre dans laquelle mijotaient des girolles à la crème."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fea9a1a7-da5c-4502-863a-219db9fb60b3",
                                "sense_id": "00c78871-c1fb-373c-bbf9-9e6da51aeac1",
                                "text": "El Mouria, c’est toute la forêt : il en connaît tous les sentiers, à des lieues, les cantons à muguet, les champs de myrtilles, les placers de girolles, de pieds rouges, de charbonniers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d27eb48f-bd50-4cc1-8579-1da307a4e152",
                                "sense_id": "00c78871-c1fb-373c-bbf9-9e6da51aeac1",
                                "text": "Près de la carrière serpentait l’ancienne route abandonnée, avec ses nombreuses ornières et à gauche la pente du petit bois où l’on cherchait quelques champignons : girolles et cèpes, amanites oronges comestibles voisinant avec des espèces vénéneuses, fausses oronges ou amanites tue-mouche dont j’aimais tant la couleur rouge du chapeau tacheté de blanc."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4b7a16db-9956-3a73-8a66-e8ef8579000b",
                        "entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ustensile servant à racler des lamelles de tête de moine (fromage suisse) ou des fromages de forme cylindrique à pâte dure comme certains fromages basques."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "22fd25e9-5ad1-4416-a613-c1e0b5659e55",
                        "source_entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "source_sense_description": "Champignon",
                        "target_lang_word": "Echte Pfifferling",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c92f4b2f-0294-4842-b2d8-17dfee1ac91f",
                        "source_entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "source_sense_description": "Champignon",
                        "target_lang_word": "Rehling",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5a44c9d3-4e11-43be-a71b-78971645c322",
                        "source_entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "source_sense_description": "Champignon",
                        "target_lang_word": "chanterelle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chanterelle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0666ec29-8b02-3d3d-b3ab-be49b5f2f679",
                                        "entry_id": "8c6ca2b1-5541-3e4f-9753-75fe5dce5cc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A widely distributed edible mushroom, Cantharellus cibarius, being yellow and trumpet-shaped; or any similar mushroom of the genera Cantharellus, Polyozellus or Gomphus, not all of which are edible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c067393d-aa1b-44de-9896-e732a3c48dd3",
                                                "sense_id": "0666ec29-8b02-3d3d-b3ab-be49b5f2f679",
                                                "text": "Even the homely wood blewits, that you cook like tripe, with milk and onions, and the egg-yolk yellow chanterelle with its fan-vaulting and faint smell of apricots, all spring up overnight like bubbles of earth, unsustained by nature, existing in a void."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bda8136e-ad2c-320d-9d3b-6d930664f938",
                                        "entry_id": "8c6ca2b1-5541-3e4f-9753-75fe5dce5cc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The highest string of the violin or similar instrument."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0768f14f-c155-4399-8752-a2cd14f45c6a",
                                                "sense_id": "bda8136e-ad2c-320d-9d3b-6d930664f938",
                                                "text": "There were hushed moments of complete beauty when the melody moved out and hung above the chanterelle like a hummingbird poised over a flower."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1f972cf5-fe34-4c42-a143-224c68a013b0",
                        "source_entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "source_sense_description": "Champignon",
                        "target_lang_word": "golden chanterelle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb8d7cf3-0991-4550-ad6b-7874e66a8714",
                        "source_entry_id": "57821295-3e08-3eee-8f3f-d00eafb37e74",
                        "source_sense_description": "Champignon",
                        "target_lang_word": "girolle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "girolle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a1c58f8-c458-3ec6-8f54-8a08e4c8ffc7",
                                        "entry_id": "0cb5fd3f-3e9f-3d8a-b463-9e6711c50f7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "chanterelle (mushroom)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11800045-3291-4877-9091-9959bc2b442b",
                                                "sense_id": "2a1c58f8-c458-3ec6-8f54-8a08e4c8ffc7",
                                                "text": "The dominance of the squeaky-clean white button has given way to a far wider range: brown chestnuts and flat-capped portobellos, and pearly-white oysters, which really do look a bit like the oyster shells they’re named after, carotene-orange girolles, flavour-bomb dried shiitake and porcini, or delicate enoki, with their long, skinny legs and tiny caps, which are often sold in packages with buna and shiro shimejis and labelled “exotic”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
